               <p xml:id="idm186">In February 1847, Hartmann received a request from the German cantor Carl Geissler to contribute with an organ piece to a collection he intended to publish in the memory of the famous German organist and composer Christian Heinrich Rinck, who had died in August 1846. On 8 October Hartmann sent him "Langfredag" (Good Friday), and after having received the manuscript Geissler asked him to write a work for Easter Day as well. On 21 November Geissler  thanked him for a second work, possibly an earlier version of "Paaskemorgen" (Easter Morning). Apparently this collection was never published, but it seems that Geissler kept Hartmann's manuscripts. Hartmann must, however have kept a copy of "Langfredag" which is unknown today, whereas he composed a new version of "Paaskemorgen" in 1886.</p>
            </history>
